    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14910" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dūmōsus</span></b>  (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dummosus</span></b> ; old form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dusmōsus</span></b> , like
			Casmena, Casmili, etc., Liv. Andron. ap. Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 67,
			5</span></i> Müll.), a, um, adj.
		dumus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of thornbushes</i>, <i>bushy</i> (rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rupes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 1, 77</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saxa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 535</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">montes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					4, 33, 5</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">colles, id. Poët. 10, 150: arva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 2, 180</span></i>
			.</div>
